{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Healing</b> — an allusion to discipline, which heals the wound of folly; like the tree of life, from whose fruit one who eats lives many years, so too one who learns discipline from his mouth lives." "<b>And perverseness</b> — one who twists his tongue to speak folly, a breach [comes] upon his spirit; like the matter of a broken spirit, which has no remedy."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:54.390669833Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}